# Architecture & Component Rules

## Component Layers (A2)
- `src/components/ui/` — **presentational only**. No business logic, no data fetching, no state beyond local UI state. shadcn lives here.
- `src/components/feature/` — combines **logic + UI**.
- Never put API calls or TanStack Query hooks inside `ui/` components.

## Component Folder Structure (A3)
Each component is its own folder. Create files **only when that concern exists** — no empty placeholders.

```
<ComponentName>/
├── index.tsx     # JSX + wiring. Always present. One React component only.
├── model.tsx     # Types for this component.
├── helper.tsx    # Pure logic.
├── constant.tsx  # Constants.
├── action.tsx    # API writes.
└── query.tsx     # TanStack Query reads.
```

## One React component per folder (A8)
Never define a second React component in the same folder. Nest page-only children under the page folder.

## Types in `model.tsx` — Never a central `src/types/` (A4)
Every type lives in the owning folder's `model.tsx`. Never create `src/types/` or standalone `*.types.ts`.

## File Extensions — Always `.tsx` (A5)
All component-folder files use `.tsx`, even non-JSX ones (`model`, `helper`, `constant`, `action`, `query`).

## Import Alias — Always `@/` (A6)
Use `@/` for cross-folder imports. Never `../../` more than one level up.
